{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Tutorial 12: The Transformer Block",
  "description": "The production-ready transformer - one node does it all!\n\nIn Tutorial 11, you saw attention exploded into pieces.\nHere, we use the TRANSFORMER_BLOCK node - a single\noptimized component that contains:\n\n1. Multi-Head Self-Attention\n2. Add & Layer Norm (residual connection)\n3. Feed-Forward Network (Linear -> GELU -> Linear)\n4. Another Add & Layer Norm\n\nTHIS IS WHAT GPT/CLAUDE USE:\nStacks of transformer blocks, one after another.\nGPT-2 has 12 blocks. GPT-4 has ~120. Claude has many too!\n\nTRY THIS:\n1. Compare speed to the exploded view (Tutorial 11)\n2. Stack multiple blocks with the 'Stacked' example\n3. See how depth improves predictions!",
