    {
      "id": "comment-tutorial",
      "type": "COMMENT",
      "name": "Tutorial",
      "position": [
        1800,
        50
      ],
      "params": {
        "text": " THE TRANSFORMER BLOCK - Production Power!\n\nThis is the REAL transformer - the optimized version\nthat GPT, Claude, and every LLM actually uses.\n\nWHAT'S INSIDE EACH ORANGE BLOCK:\n1. Multi-Head Self-Attention\n   (what you saw exploded in Tutorial 11)\n2. Residual Connection + Layer Norm\n   x' = LayerNorm(x + Attention(x))\n3. Feed-Forward Network\n   FFN(x) = Linear(GELU(Linear(x)))\n4. Another Residual + Layer Norm\n   output = LayerNorm(x' + FFN(x'))\n\nWHY RESIDUAL CONNECTIONS?\n- Allows gradients to flow through deep networks\n- Information can 'skip' layers if needed\n- This is why we can stack 100+ blocks!\n\nWHY LAYER NORM?\n- Keeps activations stable\n- Prevents exploding/vanishing values\n- Critical for deep networks\n\nTHE DEPTH ADVANTAGE:\nNotice we have TWO transformer blocks.\nEach layer learns different patterns:\n- Layer 1: Basic syntax, word relationships\n- Layer 2: Higher-level semantics, meaning\n\nGPT-2 has 12 layers. GPT-4 has ~120!\nMore layers = more complex understanding.\n\nCOMPARE THE ATTENTION MAPS:\nBlock 1 and Block 2 show different patterns.\nThis is the model learning at multiple levels!\n\nPERFORMANCE:\nOne TRANSFORMER_BLOCK node = optimized C++/CUDA\nMuch faster than building it from scratch!",
        "width": 400,
        "show_on_start": true
      },
      "inputs": {},
      "outputs": {},
      "weights": {},
      "collapsed": false,
      "color": "#5c4a3d",
      "tags": [],
      "description": "Tutorial explanation"
    }
  ],
